// Zed keymap.
//
// vim_mode is OFF, so Zed's default keymap + the VSCode overlay already give
// you almost everything. This file is therefore deliberately tiny: it contains
// ONLY bindings that differ from the defaults and that I have checked are not
// already bound to something more useful.
//
// The earlier vim-workaround layers (space leader, F-keys) are gone. They were
// only needed because vim mode claimed the ctrl-* keys, and the F-keys were
// actively stealing the debugger bindings (f4/f5/f6/f7/f9).
//
// Before adding anything here, check the default first:
//   ctrl-shift-p -> "zed: open default keymap"
[
  {
    // Back / forward through edit locations.
    // Zed's default is ctrl-alt-- and ctrl-alt-_ , which are awkward to hit.
    // alt-left/right is the browser + JetBrains convention. The only default
    // on these keys is an internal edit-prediction debug action in a different
    // context, so nothing useful is lost.
    "context": "Pane",
    "bindings": {
      "alt-left": "pane::GoBack",
      "alt-right": "pane::GoForward"
    }
  },
  {
    // VS Code parity for line duplication vs. multi-cursor.
    //
    //   VS Code (Linux)   shift-alt-down = Copy Line Down
    //                     ctrl-alt-down  = Add Cursor Below
    //   Zed default       shift-alt-down = Add Selection Below   <- swapped
    //                     ctrl-alt-shift-down = Duplicate Line
    //
    // These four restore VS Code's meaning. Delete this block to go back to
    // Zed's arrangement.
    "context": "Editor",
    "bindings": {
      "shift-alt-down": "editor::DuplicateLineDown",
      "shift-alt-up": "editor::DuplicateLineUp",
      "ctrl-alt-down": "editor::AddSelectionBelow",
      "ctrl-alt-up": "editor::AddSelectionAbove"
    }
  }
  // A dedicated "toggle just parameter hints, leave type hints always on"
  // keybinding was tried here and abandoned — not a keybinding-conflict
  // problem in the end. editor::ToggleInlayHints only gates the whole
  // inlay-hints feature on/off; re-enabling it just restores whatever the
  // show_* settings already permit, so with show_parameter_hints: false it
  // can only ever flicker type hints, never reveal parameter hints. Zed
  // has no per-category toggle action and no generic "toggle this
  // settings.json value" keybinding mechanism (verified against the
  // settings reference and key-bindings docs). Use hover for parameter
  // info on demand, or flip show_parameter_hints in settings.json by hand
  // when you specifically want it inline for a while.
]
